.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt ARNO-CLAUDE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arno-claude
.Nd make what Claude Code learned of each project arno's
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Claude Code keeps what it learns of a project in a memory directory,
.Pa ~/.claude/projects/ Ns Ar name Ns Pa /memory ,
one file a fact, and a repository may hold rules for parts of it in
.Pa .claude/rules .
.Xr arno 1
reads neither.
.Nm
writes them into arno's own context file for each project, which arno
reads last, after the project's own:
.Pa ~/.local/share/arno/projects/ Ns Ar root Ns Pa /AGENTS.md .
.Pp
For each memory directory,
.Nm
takes the repository the sessions beside it ran in, as the first of them
that records its working directory says, and writes a file for every
worktree of that repository, so that a new worktree gets the
repository's memory on the next run.
Worktrees under
.Pa ~/.cache
and
.Pa /tmp ,
such as arno's own copies of a project, are left out; so is a bare
repository.
The file holds each memory entry, its name, its description and its text,
then a line for each rule in the worktree's
.Pa .claude/rules :
the paths it is for, from its
.Ql paths:
line, and where to read it.
.Pp
The file is
.Nm Ns 's
alone: it is written whole on every run, to a temporary renamed over it,
so change the memory or the rules, not the file.
Nothing is written into a repository, and arno knows nothing of Claude
Code's files.
.Pp
.Pa arno-claude.timer ,
a systemd user timer, runs it every hour; it can be run by hand at any
time.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.claude/projects/*/memory/*.md
Claude Code's memory entries, each with front matter giving its name and
description;
.Pa MEMORY.md ,
the index, is left out.
.It Pa ~/.local/share/arno/projects/ Ns Ar root Ns Pa /AGENTS.md
What it writes, under
.Ev XDG_DATA_HOME
if that is set.
.It Pa ~/.config/systemd/user/arno-claude.service , arno-claude.timer
The hourly run, installed by arno's
.Ic make install
and turned on once with
.Ic systemctl --user enable --now arno-claude.timer .
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0, or 2 if concha stopped on an error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr arno 1 ,
.Xr concha 1
